var(--muted)">About $315</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $535,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $400 for a house</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $665,000 for a house</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Trace</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$95</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $300,000</td></tr><tr class="c3-self"><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:700">Seasons at Prince Creek West</strong></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Murrells Inlet</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $340</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $500,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1.2rem;margin:1.6rem 0 1.2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-ink);font-weight:600;margin:0 0 .4rem">From our files</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An agent at Chapter3 helped clients who owned a house in Blackmoor, a golf neighborhood in Murrells Inlet with no age rule. They sold that house and bought in Seasons, a few minutes away.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-pros-and-cons-of-living-in-seasons-at-prince"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Seasons at Prince Creek West has a gate, two pools and stores close by.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>There is a gate at the main entrance, with a call box for visitors.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Publix and the hospital are each less than 10 minutes away by car.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The Murrells Inlet MarshWalk is about 10 minutes away by car.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is a drive, not a walk. The nearest beach access is in Garden City.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Golf carts must be parked in the garage, not on the street.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>On some lots, one corner touches the high-risk flood zone. <span class="c3-pc-do">An agent checks the flood map for the house you like before you offer.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="will-a-seasons-lot-need-flood-insurance"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Will a Seasons lot need flood insurance?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most Seasons lots will not. On 45 of the lots, one corner touches the high-risk flood zone on <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=130%20Grand%20Cypress%20Way%2C%20Murrells%20Inlet%2C%20SC%2029576" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the federal flood map</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the house itself is in the zone, your lender will require flood insurance. Outside the zone, flood insurance is your choice. A policy here usually costs about $600 a year.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Carol and Jim are moving from Buffalo, and they want a house in Seasons that backs onto the woods. They find one they like and plan to make an offer that night.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">First, their Chapter3 agent checks the government's flood map for that house. The back of the house is in the high-risk flood area, so their lender will require flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">That is a yearly bill Carol and Jim had not planned on. The agent gets them a quote that afternoon, and they make their offer that night knowing the cost.</p></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get a flood insurance quote on the lot you like.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the home you are looking at. One of our agents can help you get a flood <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a> quote on it before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get a flood quote</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="seasons-at-prince-creek-west-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Seasons at Prince Creek West FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Seasons at Prince Creek West a gated community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. There is a gate at the main entrance, with a call box for visitors.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is the HOA fee in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee is about $340 a month. It includes internet, weekly trash pickup and lawn care.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are there new homes for sale in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The builder has finished, so every home for sale in Seasons is a resale.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can someone under 55 live in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if a resident 55 or older also lives in the home. No one under 18 can live there.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How old are the homes in Seasons at Prince Creek West?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes were built from 2006 to 2016. Most are on one level, with 3 bedrooms.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Seasons at Prince Creek West from the beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 13 minutes by car without traffic, to the nearest public beach access with parking, in Garden City.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.seasons55.com/editor_upload/File/Community%20Management/Policies%20%26%20Rules/communitycharter2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA rules</a>, <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/details/hospital/420098/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tidelands Waccamaw on Medicare Care Compare</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deed records</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=130%20Grand%20Cypress%20Way%2C%20Murrells%20Inlet%2C%20SC%2029576" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Federal flood insurance law</a>. For education, not legal advice. The HOA fee, the gate and the home sizes are from recent home listings. Drive times are no-traffic estimates from OpenStreetMap. The flood cost is the middle FEMA policy price in ZIP code 29576.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The clubhouse from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added the labels and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Fishing boats at a marina in Murrells Inlet. Photo: Pollinator, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murrells_inlet2473.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Seasons at Prince Creek West from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added the labels and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Homes around a pond in Seasons at Prince Creek West, from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a close view of one street from the aerial photo and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-clubhouse-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/seasons-at-prince-creek-west-clubhouse-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The clubhouse from above","caption":"The clubhouse from above.","description":"The Seasons at Prince Creek West clubhouse from above, with its outdoor pool, parking lot and tennis courts among the trees, and the entrance road marked","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"USDA Farm Service Agency, NAI