 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/common-mistakes/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I skip the inspection to make my offer stronger?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. We have watched a buyer skip it, drain her savings to about $4,000 at closing, and then face an expensive well repair she could have negotiated or walked away from. An inspection covering infestations, structure, plumbing, and electrical costs a few hundred dollars and buys you bargaining power and warning. It is the last money you should ever cut."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the most common mistake Myrtle Beach buyers make?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Skipping condo and HOA document review. Many Grand Strand buildings carry special assessments, rental restrictions, or insurance issues that only show up in the documents, and missed details become the buyer's problem after closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do out-of-state buyers make different mistakes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The most frequent are underestimating insurance costs in flood zones, assuming property taxes work like their home state, and writing an offer on a condotel before confirming it can be financed."}}]}</script>
