 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/cost-to-own/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to own a home in Myrtle Beach each month?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Add five lines: the loan payment, property taxes, insurance, HOA dues, and upkeep. The mix moves a lot between a condo and a house and between a primary home and a rental, which is what the calculator on this page is for."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is PITI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Principal, interest, taxes, and insurance, the four pieces most lenders count in your housing payment. HOA dues and upkeep sit on top of PITI, and on the coast they matter."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the calculator figure property taxes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It uses Horry County's 2026 certified millage for the location you pick and the 4 percent or 6 percent assessment based on how you will own the home. It also applies the Act 388 school exemption for legal residences and the Myrtle Beach TDF credit. It is the same model as our property tax page, where the full detail lives."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I enter for insurance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your best current estimate for the specific home, because coastal quotes vary widely by distance to water, elevation, and roof age. Wind, hail, and flood can be separate policies. Our coastal insurance page explains the pieces, and quotes during due diligence give you the real number."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a condo cheaper to own than a house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often the purchase price is lower but the HOA dues are higher, because the dues carry the building insurance and exterior upkeep. A house trades dues for direct insurance and maintenance costs. Run both through the calculator before deciding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much should I budget for maintenance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Budget about 1 percent of the home value a year, more for older homes and salt-air exposure. It is a planning number, not a bill, but the money gets spent eventually."}}]}</script>
