-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/#article","headline":"Moving From Ohio to Myrtle Beach","description":"What changes moving from Ohio to Myrtle Beach: the city income taxes you leave, the vehicle tax you gain, the retiree math, and the Ohio residency rules.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#devin-day"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-08-24","dateModified":"2026-10-04","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Moving From Ohio to Myrtle Beach"},"keywords":"moving from Ohio to Myrtle Beach, Ohio to South Carolina relocation, Ohio retirees moving to Myrtle Beach"}</script>
-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach cheaper than Ohio?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Mostly, not entirely. You stop paying local income tax, gas costs about 10 cents less, and property tax rates are far lower. Against that, a typical house costs more than the Cleveland area, sales tax is higher, and the yearly car tax is new. The calculator on our cost of living page runs your exact city."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay local income tax in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. South Carolina has no city or school district income tax anywhere. Most Ohio cities charge 1 to 3 percent of wages, so for working households this is usually the biggest single change."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is retirement income taxed in South Carolina compared with Ohio?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Ohio taxes pensions and retirement account withdrawals with credits that top out at $200 a year. South Carolina allows a deduction instead: up to $15,000 of income per person from age 65, with the retirement income deduction of up to $10,000 counting against that same $15,000. Social Security is untaxed in both."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax my car every year?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Vehicles are taxed yearly on value: a $30,000 car is taxed roughly $360 to $460 plus a $50 road fee, and the bill must be paid before the plate renews. Ohio charges a flat fee of roughly $36 to $74. Add a one-time $250 fee per vehicle when you arrive, within 45 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Ohio still tax me after I move to South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can if the move is not clean. Holding an Ohio driver's license at any point in the year, spending 213 or more day-pairs back in Ohio, or missing the October 15 non-residency statement each keep Ohio's claim alive. A snowbird split between the two states should bring in a CPA first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What surprised Devin most after moving from Ohio?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The county vehicle bill, which Ohio never sends: every vehicle here is taxed on its value each year. Then two he did not see coming: needing sunglasses daily in summer, and a job market far wider than Pleasant City, the village of about 400 he left."}}]}</script>
