 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/getting-around/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Myrtle Beach have an airport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, inside the city. Myrtle Beach International had ten airlines and nonstop service to more than 50 cities as of August 2026, and 3.8 million passengers in 2024, the last full year it has published. A terminal expansion opened in December 2025."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a car in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Plan on one. The public bus runs seven days a week and covers the main towns, but routes are limited and most daily life here is built around driving. Many neighborhoods also allow golf carts on local streets, with a permit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there public transportation in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Coast RTA runs ten fixed bus routes seven days a week, 362 days a year, serving Myrtle Beach, Conway, Surfside Beach, Garden City, Murrells Inlet, Pawleys Island, Georgetown, Loris and more. Fares are about a dollar a ride; check the current table on their site. Every bus is wheelchair accessible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is I-73 to Myrtle Beach built yet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. As of 2026 no segment of I-73 in South Carolina is open or under construction. The state is buying right of way between I-95 and the coast, and the county has set aside conditional matching money, but no construction contract exists. Treat any completion date you hear as a guess."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between US 17 Business and US 17 Bypass?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two parallel roads. Business is Kings Highway, the older road near the ocean with stoplights and driveways. The Bypass is the divided highway inland of it, carrying much more traffic: its busiest stretch counted 82,200 vehicles a day in 2025, the highest in the county. SC 31 runs even further inland with almost no lights."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is Myrtle Beach from Charleston or Charlotte?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Measured on the road network with no traffic: Charleston is about 98 miles and 2 hours 15 minutes, and Wilmington about 74 miles and 1 hour 45. Charlotte is about 170 miles and 3 hours 40, Raleigh about 186 miles and 3 hours 45, and Columbia about 138 miles and 3 hours 5."}}]}</script>
