-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to visit Myrtle Beach before buying?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily before making an offer, but we strongly recommend one in-person visit before closing. We do live video walkthroughs of neighborhoods and properties before you travel so the trip is efficient. Most of our out-of-state buyers find their home on a single 2-day visit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does a remote closing work in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SC law allows remote closings. You sign documents through a notary in your home state and submit them electronically to the closing attorney in South Carolina. We coordinate between the closing attorney, your lender, and you, so no step gets missed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Myrtle Beach neighborhoods are best for relocators?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Carolina Forest is the most popular landing spot for families relocating to the Grand Strand. It has the best schools in Horry County, approximately 30 sub-neighborhoods across a range of price points, and an active resale market. Market Common is the top pick for professionals who want walkability. Murrells Inlet and Pawleys Island attract those looking for a quieter lifestyle away from the tourist corridor."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is Myrtle Beach's cost of living compared to the Northeast?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Overall cost of living in Myrtle Beach runs approximately 7% below the national average. Housing is significantly lower than markets in NC, NY, NJ, and PA. There is no state income tax on Social Security in SC, and property taxes are among the lowest in the region. The main cost surprises are coastal insurance and HOA fees on condos, which buyers from inland markets do not expect."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I know about schools in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"School quality varies significantly by location in Horry County. Carolina Forest has the strongest school performance, including River Oaks Elementary and Carolina Forest High. Conway, Socastee, and Saint James districts are also solid options. Myrtle Beach city schools trend lower in performance ratings. If schools are a priority, filter your search to the Carolina Forest and North Myrtle Beach areas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Buying in the wrong neighborhood for their lifestyle","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Grand Strand is not one market. A family relocating from the suburbs of Charlotte who buys an oceanfront condo in Myrtle Beach city often finds the area too touristy and lacking the suburban feel they expected. Spend time in multiple neighborhoods on your visit before narrowing down. We build a neighborhood tour into every relocation plan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Underestimating coastal insurance costs","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Buyers from inland markets are accustomed to one homeowners insurance policy. In coastal SC you need three: homeowners, wind/hail, and flood. Together these can add $400 to $700 per month to your housing cost. Get insurance quotes during your due diligence period, not after."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Not getting pre-approved before shopping","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Out-of-state buyers sometimes start touring before completing their pre-approval, assuming they can transfer a pre-approval letter from their current state. SC lenders underwrite coastal properties differently, particularly for condos, flood-zone properties, and investment purchases. Get your pre-approval with a SC-licensed lender before you tour. Our preferred lender, BrickWood Mortgage, is SC-licensed and can pre-approve you directly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Relying on Zillow neighborhood data instead of local knowledge","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Zillow's neighborhood ratings do not reflect the block-by-block differences in the Grand Strand market. A zip code that looks average in the statistics may contain a top-rated school district, a golf-cart-friendly community, or a high-performing STR corridor. Ask your agent for a block-by-block breakdown before drawing conclusions from online ratings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy a home while I'm still relocating from out of state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, most of our relocating buyers start from hundreds of miles away. We handle video walkthroughs, local due diligence, and the paperwork remotely so you can make a confident offer without flying down for every showing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a mortgage if I'm changing jobs to move here?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often yes, but a new job or an income gap can complicate qualifying. Because our lending partner, BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497), works with us daily, the loan timing and the contract timing can move together, and we've negotiated contract extensions with sellers to buy clients time to get their income in place."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do most people relocating to Myrtle Beach come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"North Carolina is the single biggest state we see, since it sits right next door. After that, the largest groups come from the Northeast, mainly New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania, plus Ohio. Most are moving for the coast, the lower taxes and cost of living, and a slower pace."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are property taxes lower in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a primary residence, usually yes. Owner-occupied homes in South Carolina are assessed at 4 percent and exempt from school operating taxes, which keeps effective rates among the lowest in the country."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy in Myrtle Beach before I move?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Remote purchases are routine on the Grand Strand, with video tours, digital signing, and a mail-away or remote closing coordinated through a South Carolina attorney."}}]}</script>
