cense and to register every vehicle you own. The DMV charges about $305 per car, and the county charges its annual vehicle tax before the DMV will hand you a plate. Second, the 4 percent legal residence application for your new home, which Horry County wants by May 31; without it your first property tax bill is calculated at the 6 percent second-home rate. Third, voter registration, which closes 30 days before any election.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">Devin, who wrote this page, moved here from Ohio three years ago, missed the 45 day license window, and did not learn about the free resident beach parking until his second year. This is the checklist he wishes someone had handed him.</p></div></section>
