 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The four seasons, from the official station</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are 1991 to 2020 normals from the North Myrtle Beach airport station, the one the National Weather Service uses for this coast&#39;s official records. A normal is a thirty year average, so a given week will run above or below it.</p>
