 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Four things to compare before you pick a town</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">People search Myrtle Beach and then buy somewhere else on this list, because the name covers about sixty miles of coast plus the inland towns behind it. Compare these four differences first.</p><div class="wt-grid"><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">1</span><span class="wt-t">City limits, or unincorporated county</span><span class="wt-d">Incorporated towns set their own sales tax, trash pickup, parking decals, zoning, golf cart and rental rules. Unincorporated areas follow county rules for all of it.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">2</span><span class="wt-t">What your budget reaches</span><span class="wt-d">The starting price in Conway and the starting price on Pawleys Island are more than $300,000 apart for similar houses.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">3</span><span class="wt-t">Has special features you like</span><span class="wt-d">Marinas. Golf. A fishing pier. Acreage. Marsh views. New construction. Historic streets. Beach houses. The table below has each area&#39;s.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">4</span><span class="wt-t">The drive</span><span class="wt-d">Is the location close enough to everything you need? Work, the airport, the stores you go to weekly. Measure it before you offer.</span></div></div><style>.wt-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:1px;background:var(--rule);border:1px solid var(--rule);max-width:900px;margin-top:.4rem}.wt-cell{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.