 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is everyone moving to Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The same four reasons, in different orders. A typical home is near $342,000 while the places movers come from average $418,000 to $669,000. South Carolina taxes are among the lowest in the country for a primary home. The coast stays warm into October. There is enough growth that work and new construction keep up. The IRS counted about 15,000 households moving into Horry County in a single year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach growing that fast?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Census Bureau ranked this metro among the fastest growing in the country in its March 2026 release. Employment here grew 9.1 percent from 2019 to 2025 against 5.1 percent nationally. The households arriving reported about 2.5 times the income of the households leaving on the IRS migration file."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do most people moving to Myrtle Beach come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"North Carolina is the single biggest source, right next door. After that come New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Ohio, Maryland, Virginia, Connecticut and Massachusetts. We wrote a full tax and price comparison for each of those moves, state by state."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a good place to live year round?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most of our buyers, yes, and we keep an honest page on exactly that question, including the parts people leave over: summers are humid, a quarter of the jobs follow the tourist season, and you will want a car. The beach, the prices and the taxes are what they stay for."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do retirees move to Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Social Security is never taxed in South Carolina at any income, and retirement deductions here have no income test. Military retirement is fully exempt, owner-occupied property tax is among the lowest in the country, and there is no estate or inheritance tax. Then the ocean stays warm enough to swim into October."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are investors buying in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Millions of visitors a year rent somewhere to sleep, and oceanfront condos sell at prices northern buyers compare with parking spaces back home. Our Airbnb income page carries the real revenue ranges from five data vendors, and the building directory shows which buildings finance."}}]}</script>
