irs collects HOA complaints because the law requires it, and publishes an annual report. But it does not administer or enforce the Homeowners Association Act, and its complaint process is voluntary mediation. It cannot force an association to participate or require any outcome."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I get the HOA documents before I buy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You should, and most buyers do not. In the state's 2026 report only 32 percent of complainants said they received the governing documents before purchase, while 53 percent got them after. Reading them first is the purpose of the review we run."}}]}</script>
