ont-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Is there a limit on how many rentals you can finance?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on standard loans, and almost nobody reaches it. <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b2-2-03/multiple-financed-properties-same-borrower" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The standard limit is ten financed properties</a>, counting your own home if it has a mortgage. Investors who pass it use <a href="/invest/strategies/dscr-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">DSCR loans</a> or portfolio loans, which have no such limit. Most investors never think about it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How much do lenders want in reserves for a second rental?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Reserves are money in your accounts on the day the loan closes. The lender does not take it, hold it or freeze it. You prove it is there with statements, and you keep it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b3-4.1-01/minimum-reserve-requirements" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The standard rule asks for six months of the new property's payment</a>: principal, interest, taxes, insurance and dues. It also asks for a small share of the loan balances on your other financed rentals. <a href="https://www.pinnaclefundingnetwork.com/blog/32-dscr-loan-reserve-requirements.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A DSCR lender writes its own rule</a>. Most ask for two to six months of the new payment. Some add a few months for each other rental you own. Ask for the figure before you shop. <a href="/invest/cash-to-close/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What lender reserves are, and what else you pay at closing</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Ready for the next one?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">One call. We run the next house and put you with a loan officer at our preferred lender.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Second rental FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the most common mistake when buying a second rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Spending the reserve. The house takes every dollar, and the first empty month or the first repair has nothing to pay it. Keep the reserve, buy fewer houses if you must, and keep buying.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use equity from one rental to buy another in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A cash-out refinance or a line of credit on a property you own can pay the next down payment, so the purchase takes no new cash from savings. Both loans then depend on the rents. The rent on each house must pay that house's loan.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does the lender hold my reserves?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Reserves are money you prove is in your accounts when the loan closes. The lender does not take it or freeze it. You keep it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is there a limit on how many rentals I can finance?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On standard loans, ten financed properties, counting your own home. Almost nobody reaches it. Investors who do use DSCR or portfolio loans, which have no such limit.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b2-2-03/multiple-financed-properties-same-borrower" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae Selling Guide, multiple financed properties</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b3-4.1-01/minimum-reserve-requirements" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Selling Guide, minimum reserves</a>, <a href="https://www.pinnaclefundingnetwork.com/blog/32-dscr-loan-reserve-requirements.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A DSCR lender's published reserve guideline</a>. Read September 7, 2026. Educational only, not a loan offer. Chapter3 is a real estate brokerage. Loan rules change; a loan officer confirms them for your file.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying your second rental in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">One call. We run the rent on the next house and check the numbers with both loans on them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></section></main>
