 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a property manager for a Myrtle Beach rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. An owner may manage their own property without a license. A manager makes sense when you live elsewhere, when the building has a rental desk, or when you do not want the calls."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What license must a property manager have in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A real estate broker license or a property manager license, and they must work under a broker-in-charge or property manager-in-charge who is responsible for the trust account."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is my tenant's security deposit kept?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the manager's trust account until the lease ends. State law requires it. When the tenant leaves, any deduction must be itemized in writing within 30 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the accommodations tax when a manager books the guest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The manager, on the full booking, because the manager takes the payment. You remit the tax only on stays you book yourself, and then you need a retail license."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the management agreement renew automatically?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only with a clause that lets either side cancel on 30 days' notice after the first term ends. State law requires that clause."}}]}</script>
