 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to join the building's rental program?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if the building's recorded documents require it. Many programs are voluntary. The agreement and the master deed say which. We read both before you offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use Airbnb while I am in the program?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Check the exclusivity clause. Some agreements allow outside bookings with notice and some do not."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the accommodations tax when the program books the guest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The program does, on the full booking, because it takes the payment. If you book a guest yourself, you remit that stay's tax and need a retail license."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does joining a rental program affect my loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can. A lender treats a building that requires pooling, limits owner use, or shares rental profit with the manager as a hotel-type project. Those units need a condotel or portfolio loan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I ask the program for before I offer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The agreement, the fee schedule, and the last twelve months of owner statements for the unit or a similar one. Also the owner-use rules and the exit terms."}}]}</script>
