 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a state retail license for my short-term rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if you take bookings and payments yourself. If every booking runs through a manager or a platform that takes the payment, they remit the tax and you need no state license."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Airbnb pay all my taxes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It collects the state taxes and the local taxes it lists for your area. You remit any local fee it does not list, and everything on stays you book yourself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a business license for a rental in the City of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The city requires one for every rental property, short-term or long-term, and a zoning check comes first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the personal property return?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A yearly form to the county auditor listing the furnishings in a rental that is not your legal residence. The county then bills a tax on them in the fall."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent nightly in a residential neighborhood in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Almost never. Most residential zones in the city do not allow stays under 90 days. A 90-day lease is allowed there."}}]}</script>
