 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell a house with a tenant in it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The lease continues and the buyer becomes the landlord at closing. Give the tenant written notice of the sale and transfer the deposit to the buyer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my rental to a buyer with an FHA, VA or USDA loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if the tenant will be out within about 60 days of closing, because most lenders require the buyer to move in within 60 days on those loans. With more months left on the lease, the buyer is an investor, or you wait for the lease to end, or you pay the tenant to leave."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I evict my tenant so I can sell?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Selling is not one of the three grounds for ejectment. A month-to-month tenancy ends on 30 days written notice. A fixed lease runs to its end date or ends by a paid buyout."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much notice do I give a tenant for a showing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At least 24 hours, at reasonable times. The tenant cannot unreasonably refuse, and you cannot use showings to harass."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to my Airbnb bookings when I sell?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The buyer takes the property subject to every booking that starts within 90 days of the deed being recorded, and to the management agreement for those stays. Later guests get a refund within 45 days. You must disclose every future booking in writing before the contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does South Carolina withhold from an out-of-state seller?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The top individual income tax rate, which is 5.21 percent for a 2026 sale. It applies to the gain if you give the buyer a signed affidavit of gain, or to the whole sale price if you do not. It is a prepayment credited on your state return."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay tax on depreciation when I sell a rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The gain from depreciation is taxed at up to 25 percent, and the rest at capital gains rates. A 1031 exchange defers both if you identify a replacement within 45 days and close within 180."}}]}</script>
