ight:600;text-decoration:none">Little River</a></td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy)">Long-term rental</td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$12,243</td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">30.3%</td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$202</td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">171</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy)"><a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Carolina Forest</a></td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy)">Long-term rental</td><td style="padding:.6rem .85rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums" colspan="4"><span style="color:var(--muted);font-style:italic">No nightly-rental market; judge it on yearly rent and schools</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem;margin-top:.9rem">AirROI, data through 2026-08-08. Carolina Forest checked the same day and has no published market.</p><div style="margin-top:2.75rem"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.5rem">Start here</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.7rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Start from what you are trying to do</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:.4rem">Nine submarkets is a lot to read through. Find the line that matches your plan and start on that page.</p><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the highest nightly revenue per property</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Murrells Inlet</a> and <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Surfside Beach</a>. They lead the Strand on average annual revenue and nightly rate, because the south end is mostly whole houses rather than one- and two-bedroom condos.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the lowest price to get in</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Conway</a> and <a href="/submarkets/little-river/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Little River</a>. Both are yearly-rental markets inland or up the coast, with the lowest entry prices on the Strand and tenant demand that does not depend on the summer.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want schools and a family neighborhood</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Carolina Forest</a>. It is the master-planned inland corridor, the HOAs require long leases rather than nightly stays, and tenant demand follows the school attendance zones.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the easiest property to buy, rent and resell</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Myrtle Beach</a> or <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">North Myrtle Beach</a>. They hold the great majority of the Strand&#39;s listings, so there is always inventory, always comparable sales, and always a buyer when you sell.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want quiet, and I am buying for myself as much as for yield</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Pawleys Island</a>. Higher nightly rates, lower occupancy, an older and higher-end housing stock, and a buyer pool motivated as much by using the place as renting it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want to be near the water without oceanfront pricing</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Garden City</a>. The peninsula has ocean on one side and the inlet on the other, and creek-side homes with dock access sit well below the oceanfront blocks.</p></div></div></div></section>
