 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Myrtle Beach good for short-term rentals?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It has the region's deepest tourist demand, especially near the oceanfront, though performance and short-term-rental rules vary by area and building."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What property types are common in Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A broad mix, from oceanfront and resort condominiums to single-family neighborhoods inland."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you short-term rental (Airbnb) a house in Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Usually not. The City of Myrtle Beach prohibits rentals under 90 days in all R (residential) zoning districts except RMV, and treats STRs as a commercial use. You generally need a property in an STR-eligible tourist or RMV zone and a business license. Lodging taxes and fees on the rent total 13 percent inside the city."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What counts as a short-term rental in Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The city defines a short-term rental as any stay under 90 days. South Carolina uses the same 90-day line for its lodging tax."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's or seller's market?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It leans toward buyers in early-to-mid 2026, especially in the condo segment, where inventory sits around seven to eight months of supply and gives buyers negotiating room."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are property taxes on a second home in Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Higher than on a primary residence. A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In the city of Myrtle Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3.8 times a primary home's on the same house."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which schools serve Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Public schools fall within the Myrtle Beach attendance area of Horry County Schools. Assignment is by address, and Chapter3 will confirm the exact schools on the district boundary map."}}]}</script>
